# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A venv is machine- and platform-specific: its config hardcodes absolute paths
# and its site-packages holds compiled wheels for one OS and CPU. It must never
# be committed — each developer runs setup.sh instead.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# ── Python bytecode and build artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Test and type-checker caches ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# ── Generated figures, animations and datasets ────────────────────────────────
# The figures, per-trial Monte Carlo records (mc_*.csv) and mc_tables.tex behind
# the paper ARE tracked, so the published numbers can be checked without a rerun
# (see reproduce/).  Animations are large and regenerate with `main.py animate`.
outputs/*.gif
outputs/*.mp4
outputs/test_dataset*/
outputs_before_rerun_*/
out/

# ── Private working material (kept locally, never published) ──────────────────
# Manuscript drafts, journal-submission packages and superseded code.
idea/
idea_backup_*/
_superseded/
asr/
asr_resubmit/
zenodo/
Claude outputs/
*.bak_*

# ── LaTeX build products ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.lof
*.log
*.lot
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc

# ── Editors and OS cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .idea/ holds PyCharm's per-machine interpreter path, so it is excluded; if you
# want to share run configurations, commit .idea/runConfigurations/ explicitly.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── reproduce/ run products (regenerated by reproduce/rerun_all.sh) ───────────
reproduce/logs/
reproduce/claims_report.txt
